{"id":"voneinander","lemma":"voneinander","pos":"adv","rank":3965,"glosses":["from / of one another, from / of each other"],"audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/2e/De-voneinander.ogg/De-voneinander.ogg.mp3","examples":[{"text":"Was wissen Sie voneinander?","en":"What do you know about each other?","words":[{"g":"what"},{"g":"to know"},{"g":"she / they / you"},null]},{"text":"Wir könnten viel voneinander lernen.","en":"We could learn a lot from each other.","words":[{"g":"we"},{"g":"can, to be able to","l":"können"},{"g":"much, a lot"},null,{"g":"to learn"}]},{"text":"Wir hatten genug voneinander.","en":"We'd had enough of each other.","words":[{"g":"we"},{"g":"to have","l":"haben"},{"g":"enough"},null]},{"text":"Wir brauchen eine Pause voneinander.","en":"We need to take a break from each other.","words":[{"g":"we"},{"g":"to need"},{"g":"a"},{"g":"pause"},null]},{"text":"Sie sind voneinander enttäuscht.","en":"They are disappointed with each other.","words":[{"g":"she / they / you"},{"g":"are","l":"sein"},null,{"g":"disappointed"}]}]}